:: False Sympathy [event mom_quest] {"position":"3275,950","size":"100,100"}
The front door flies open hard enough to bounce off the wall. I'm in the hallway, leaning on the banister with my phone, and I've been pretending to scroll the same three posts for the last twenty minutes. I already know what's coming. Knowing doesn't stop my heart from speeding up.

$mom.callName comes in with her bag hanging off one arm and her keys still in her hand. Her mascara has run and dried and run again. The blouse I talked her into is wrinkled now, one side untucked, like she spent the afternoon hunched over something. Probably a cardboard box.

She drops the bag on the floor and just stands there. I put the phone away and walk over slowly, the way you'd approach someone standing on a ledge.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $mom, text: "$player.name... they fired me. They actually... I got fired." },
    { who: $player, text: "What? Hey, hey. Come here. Sit down." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
<<linkreplace "Sit down with her...">>
She sinks onto the bottom step of the stairs and puts her face in her hands. I sit down next to her. Our knees touch.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $mom, text: "He called me into his office. With the door open, so everyone could hear. He said I'd deleted client files and wrecked the schedules and lost some forecast... and I didn't, honey, I know I didn't. But it was all right there on my laptop." },
    { who: $mom, text: "He called me a liability. A liability! After all these years. And then security walked me to the elevator like I was going to steal a stapler." },
    { who: $player, text: "That's insane. You're the only reason that floor runs at all." },
    { who: $mom, text: "Tell that to him. Everyone was staring at me. Nobody said a word." },
    { text: "She takes a shaky breath and looks at the front door, like the bills might come through it any second." },
    { who: $mom, text: "And now what? The mortgage, your $sister.relation's tuition... we need that paycheck. What am I supposed to do?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She looks at me as if I might have the answer. As it happens, I do.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $player, text: "Okay. Don't panic. What if you came and worked for me?" },
    { who: $mom, text: "For you? At your... company?" },
    { who: $player, text: "I mean it. I need someone who's good with people, who can keep schedules and clients and paperwork from falling apart. That's literally what you've been doing for that idiot for years." },
    { who: $mom, text: "Sweetie, that's very sweet of you. But it's still tiny, isn't it? It's barely making anything. I can't afford to take that kind of pay cut, not right now, we need..." },
    { who: $player, text: "It won't stay tiny. And you'd be the first real employee. No one yelling at you, no one making comments about your skirt. Just the two of us building something." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She chews her lip and doesn't answer. I slide my hand into my pocket and find the dial by touch.

<<linkreplace "Switch on the prototype">>
<<Video "images/characters/player/prototype/on.mp4" "" "" 500>>
The hum is so quiet that even I almost miss it under the sound of her sniffling. <<UseQuestDevice $mom>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
    { who: $mom, text: "I don't know. It feels like a big risk." },
    { who: $player, text: "It's a smaller risk than sitting at home sending out résumés. I need you there, $mom.callName. I really do." },
    { text: "Her shoulders come down, one at a time. She wipes her cheek with her sleeve and looks at me properly for the first time since she walked in." },
    { who: $mom, text: "...You really think I'd be useful?" },
    { who: $player, text: "I know you would. Say yes." },
    { who: $mom, text: "Okay. Okay, sweetie. Yes. Thank you. I honestly don't know what I'd do without you right now." },
    { who: $player, text: "Well, you don't have to find out." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She throws her arms around me and holds on. She smells like her perfume and the office and a little bit like the rain outside. I hold her back, my hand moving in slow circles between her shoulder blades, the way she used to do for me when I was little.

She has no idea she's thanking the person who emptied her desk. I keep holding her until she stops shaking, and the prototype keeps humming in my pocket the whole time, just to be sure the decision sticks.

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 6>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 4>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "MomResistance" 6>>

<<ProfileLog $mom "My First Employee" "She got fired, right on schedule, and came home with nowhere to go. Now she works for me. She thinks I saved her.">>
<<set setup.getMealById("false_sympathie").isActive to true>>
<<NextQuest $mom>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<<silent>>
    /* fired: she stays home on weekdays from now on (Define Schedule) */
    <<run setup.useRoutine("mom", "weekday", "stage0_fired")>>
    /* no paycheck anymore, so no more $500 a week toward the rent (Weekly Update) */
    <<set $mom.flags.rentHelp to false>>

    <<set $locations[12].name to "$boss.callName's Office">>
<</silent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
